# XPS: the exit-pupil SURFACE from the full ray grid on the manual's Cassegrain with exit pupil
# (cmdref: Ray Tracing).  Needs a STOP; modifies no element.  The chief-ray crossing (the FEX vertex)
# is at z = -5.2907 with zp = 6.7907 -- the FEX radius the manual's example reports (6.790667844).
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CassWithExitPupil.in
stop obj 0 0 0
xps 5
# EXPECT: XPS: vertex =\s+0\.0+(E\+000)?\s+0\.0+(E\+000)?\s+-5\.29066784375\d+
# EXPECT: XPS: zp\(chief\) =\s+6\.79066784375\d+
# EXPECT: XPS: exit-pupil surface computed; crossings in the ray buffer
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
